IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `crtpa-kleene`
IMPORT `crtpa-nouns`

-- Contracts (Rights of Third Parties) Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal
-- consolidation -- LAYER 1, SECTION 3: VARIATION AND RESCISSION OF CONTRACT.
--
-- What is encoded: s 3(1) (the bar on the parties, with its three circumstances), (2) (the assent), (3) (express
-- terms of the contract), (4) to (6) (the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with the consent, and impose
-- conditions) and (7) (which courts).  The bar of s 3(1) is a prohibition on a named party (the parties to the
-- contract): it is encoded as a decision function and, derived from that answer, as a regulative rule (ruling N2).
--
-- READING A RESULT.  JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are answers the Act itself gives; NOTHING means the Act does not
-- answer on these facts (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING").
-- For the bar of s 3(1), JUST TRUE means "the Act says the parties may not do this", and JUST FALSE means "this
-- subsection does not bar them here"; JUST FALSE is not a statement that they are permitted.
--
-- JUDGMENTS HANDED TO OTHERS.  "can reasonably be expected to have foreseen" (s 3(1)(c)) and the satisfaction of the
-- court or tribunal (s 3(4), (5)) are inputs the person states; they are never guessed.

§ `Section 3(1) -- the three circumstances`

-- src:117 | (a) the third party has communicated the third party’s assent to
-- src:118 | the term to the promisor;
@ref s 3(1)(a) (src:117-118)
GIVEN `the third party has communicated the third party's assent to the term to the promisor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(a) the third party has communicated the third party's assent to the term to the promisor` MEANS
    `the third party has communicated the third party's assent to the term to the promisor`

-- src:120 | (b) the promisor is aware that the third party has relied on the
-- src:121 | term (whether or not the third party has knowledge of its
-- src:122 | precise terms); or
@ref s 3(1)(b) (src:120-122)
GIVEN `the promisor is aware that the third party has relied on the term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(b) the promisor is aware that the third party has relied on the term` MEANS
    `the promisor is aware that the third party has relied on the term`

-- src:124 | (c) the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen
-- src:125 | that the third party would rely on the term and the third
-- src:126 | party has in fact relied on the term (whether or not the third
-- src:127 | party has knowledge of its precise terms).
@ref s 3(1)(c) (src:124-127)
GIVEN `the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that the third party would rely on the term` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the third party has in fact relied on the term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(c) the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that the third party would rely on the term and the third party has in fact relied on it` MEANS
    `three-valued AND`
        `the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that the third party would rely on the term`
        (`a stated fact` `the third party has in fact relied on the term`)

-- (b) and (c) each say "whether or not the third party has knowledge of its precise terms": the knowledge is not a
-- condition of either, whatever the answer.
-- src:120 | (b) the promisor is aware that the third party has relied on the
-- src:121 | term (whether or not the third party has knowledge of its
-- src:122 | precise terms); or
-- src:124 | (c) the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen
-- src:125 | that the third party would rely on the term and the third
-- src:126 | party has in fact relied on the term (whether or not the third
-- src:127 | party has knowledge of its precise terms).
@ref s 3(1)(b) (src:120-122) and (c) (src:124-127)
GIVEN `the third party has knowledge of the precise terms of the term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1)(b) and (c) knowledge of the precise terms of the term is a condition` MEANS
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(whether or not the third party has knowledge of its precise terms)"
    JUST FALSE

-- src:110 | 3.—(1) Subject to this section, where a third party has a right under
-- src:111 | section 2 to enforce a term of the contract, the parties to the contract
-- src:113 | may not, by agreement, rescind the contract, or vary the contract in
-- src:114 | such a way as to extinguish or alter the third party’s entitlement under
-- src:115 | that right, without the third party’s consent if —
-- src:117 | (a) the third party has communicated the third party’s assent to
-- src:118 | the term to the promisor;
-- src:120 | (b) the promisor is aware that the third party has relied on the
-- src:121 | term (whether or not the third party has knowledge of its
-- src:122 | precise terms); or
-- src:124 | (c) the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen
-- src:125 | that the third party would rely on the term and the third
-- src:126 | party has in fact relied on the term (whether or not the third
-- src:127 | party has knowledge of its precise terms).
@ref s 3(1) the circumstances (src:115-127)
GIVEN `the third party has communicated the third party's assent to the term to the promisor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the promisor is aware that the third party has relied on the term` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that the third party would rely on the term` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the third party has in fact relied on the term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
-- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", read as the text's no within the provision that holds it; marginal reading M5): "without the third party's consent if — (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..."
-- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): when (a) and (b) are not made out and the judgment of (c) has not been stated, the answer is NOTHING
`s 3(1) one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` MEANS
    `three-valued OR`
        (`a stated fact` (`s 3(1)(a) the third party has communicated the third party's assent to the term to the promisor` `the third party has communicated the third party's assent to the term to the promisor`))
        (`three-valued OR`
            (`a stated fact` (`s 3(1)(b) the promisor is aware that the third party has relied on the term` `the promisor is aware that the third party has relied on the term`))
            (`s 3(1)(c) the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that the third party would rely on the term and the third party has in fact relied on it` `the promisor can reasonably be expected to have foreseen that the third party would rely on the term` `the third party has in fact relied on the term`))

§ `Section 3(2) -- the assent`

-- src:129 | (2) The assent mentioned in subsection (1)(a) —
-- src:131 | (a) may be by words or conduct; and
@ref s 3(2)(a) (src:129-131)
GIVEN `the form of the assent` IS A `Form of the third party's assent`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(2)(a) the assent may be by this form` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the form of the assent`
    WHEN `words` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `conduct` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be by words or conduct" is not closed with "only", so another form is neither allowed nor excluded
    WHEN `silence or inaction` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be by words or conduct" is not closed with "only", so another form is neither allowed nor excluded
    WHEN `some other form` THEN NOTHING

-- The "until" bar (ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (d)): the assent "is not to be regarded as communicated to the promisor until
-- the assent is received by the promisor".  The bar is encoded as its own yes/no, and the Act is never made to say that
-- the assent HAS been communicated.
-- src:129 | (2) The assent mentioned in subsection (1)(a) —
-- src:133 | (b) if sent to the promisor by post or other means, is not to be
-- src:134 | regarded as communicated to the promisor until the assent
-- src:135 | is received by the promisor.
@ref s 3(2)(b) (src:133-135)
GIVEN `the assent was sent to the promisor by post or other means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the promisor has received the assent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(2)(b) the assent cannot yet be regarded as communicated to the promisor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if"; marginal reading M6): "if sent to the promisor by post or other means, is not to be regarded as communicated to the promisor until the assent is received by the promisor"
        IF NOT `the assent was sent to the promisor by post or other means` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text's own "until"; ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (d)): "until the assent is received by the promisor"
        IF `the promisor has received the assent` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 3(2)(b) (src:133-135)
GIVEN `the assent was sent to the promisor by post or other means` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the promisor has received the assent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(2)(b) the assent has been communicated to the promisor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text's own "until"; ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (d)): "is not to be regarded as communicated to the promisor until the assent is received by the promisor"
        IF `the assent was sent to the promisor by post or other means` AND NOT `the promisor has received the assent` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says only when the assent is NOT regarded as communicated; it does not say that receipt is communication, or how an assent not sent by post or other means is communicated
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Section 3(1) -- the bar on the parties`

-- JUST TRUE: "the parties to the contract may not, by agreement, rescind the contract, or vary the contract in such a way
-- as to extinguish or alter the third party's entitlement under that right, without the third party's consent".
-- src:110 | 3.—(1) Subject to this section, where a third party has a right under
-- src:111 | section 2 to enforce a term of the contract, the parties to the contract
-- src:113 | may not, by agreement, rescind the contract, or vary the contract in
-- src:114 | such a way as to extinguish or alter the third party’s entitlement under
-- src:115 | that right, without the third party’s consent if —
@ref s 3(1) (src:110-115)
GIVEN `the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce the term` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `what the parties do` IS A `What the parties do by agreement`
      `the third party has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on the parties acting "by agreement" and to "rescind the contract, or vary the contract in such a way as to extinguish or alter the third party's entitlement"; another change is outside it
        IF `what the parties do` EQUALS `vary the contract in some other way` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on the parties acting "by agreement" and to "rescind the contract, or vary the contract in such a way as to extinguish or alter the third party's entitlement"; another change is outside it
        IF `what the parties do` EQUALS `change the contract otherwise than by agreement of the parties` THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on acting "without the third party's consent"; with consent it does not speak
        IF `the third party has consented` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; the periods-and-where ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)): "where a third party has a right under section 2 to enforce a term of the contract"
        IF `the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce the term` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if"; marginal reading M5): "without the third party's consent if — (a) ...; (b) ...; or (c) ..."
        IF `one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- TRUE: the text's own "may not"
        IF `the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce the term` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): whether the third party has a right under section 2, or whether a circumstance exists, has not been stated
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Section 3(3) -- express terms of the contract`

-- "Subsection (1) is subject to any express term of the contract under which —": (a) the parties may rescind or vary
-- without the consent, or (b) the consent is required in circumstances the contract specifies instead of (1)(a), (b), (c).
-- src:137 | (3) Subsection (1) is subject to any express term of the contract
-- src:138 | under which —
-- src:140 | (a) the parties to the contract may by agreement rescind or
-- src:141 | vary the contract without the consent of the third party; or
-- src:143 | (b) the consent of the third party is required in circumstances
-- src:144 | specified in the contract instead of those set out in
-- src:145 | subsection (1)(a), (b) and (c).
@ref s 3(3) (src:137-145)
GIVEN `the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce the term` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `what the parties do` IS A `What the parties do by agreement`
      `the third party has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the express term of the contract about consent` IS AN `Express term of the contract about consent`
      `the circumstances the contract specifies exist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(1) with (3) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent, taking an express term of the contract into account` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the express term of the contract about consent`
    WHEN `a term under which the parties may rescind or vary without the third party's consent` THEN
        -- FALSE-kind ("subject to" read as the text's no, marginal reading M3): "Subsection (1) is subject to any express term of the contract under which — (a) the parties to the contract may by agreement rescind or vary the contract without the consent of the third party"
        IF `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` `the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce the term` `what the parties do` `the third party has consented` `one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` `the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce the term` `what the parties do` `the third party has consented` `one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists`
    -- the circumstances the contract specifies take the place of (1)(a), (b) and (c): "instead of those set out in subsection (1)(a), (b) and (c)"
    WHEN `a term requiring the third party's consent in circumstances specified in the contract instead of those in section 3(1)(a), (b) and (c)` THEN
        `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` `the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce the term` `what the parties do` `the third party has consented` (`a stated fact` `the circumstances the contract specifies exist`)
    WHEN `no such express term` THEN
        `s 3(1) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` `the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce the term` `what the parties do` `the third party has consented` `one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists`

§ `Section 3(4) to (7) -- dispensing with the consent`

-- "may ... dispense with such consent if the court or tribunal is satisfied that —": the court's power, and not a duty.
-- JUST TRUE means the power exists on these facts.
-- src:147 | (4) Where the consent of a third party is required under
-- src:148 | subsection (1) or (3), the court or arbitral tribunal may, on the
-- src:149 | application of the parties to the contract, dispense with such consent if
-- src:150 | the court or tribunal is satisfied that —
-- src:152 | (a) the consent cannot be obtained because the third party’s
-- src:153 | whereabouts cannot reasonably be ascertained; or
-- src:160 | (b) the third party is mentally incapable of giving the third
-- src:161 | party’s consent.
@ref s 3(4) (src:147-161)
GIVEN `the consent of the third party is required under subsection (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties to the contract have applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or tribunal is satisfied that the consent cannot be obtained because the third party's whereabouts cannot reasonably be ascertained` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court or tribunal is satisfied that the third party is mentally incapable of giving the third party's consent` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with the third party's consent` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "where"; the periods-and-where ruling of 2026-11-05, rule (b)): "Where the consent of a third party is required under subsection (1) or (3)"
        IF NOT `the consent of the third party is required under subsection (1) or (3)` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (an "on the application" condition read like "upon", ruling rule (c); marginal reading M7): "on the application of the parties to the contract"
        IF NOT `the parties to the contract have applied` THEN JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", marginal reading M5): "if the court or tribunal is satisfied that — (a) ...; or (b) ..."
            -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the satisfaction of the court or tribunal is a judgment handed to it, and the person has not stated it
            `three-valued OR`
                `the court or tribunal is satisfied that the consent cannot be obtained because the third party's whereabouts cannot reasonably be ascertained`
                `the court or tribunal is satisfied that the third party is mentally incapable of giving the third party's consent`

-- src:163 | (5) The court or arbitral tribunal may, on the application of the
-- src:164 | parties to a contract, dispense with any consent that may be required
-- src:165 | under subsection (1)(c) if it is satisfied that it cannot reasonably be
-- src:166 | ascertained whether or not the third party has in fact relied on the term
-- src:167 | of the contract.
@ref s 3(5) (src:163-167)
GIVEN `the consent is one that may be required under subsection (1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties to the contract have applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or tribunal is satisfied that it cannot reasonably be ascertained whether or not the third party has in fact relied on the term` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(5) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with a consent that may be required under subsection (1)(c)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over "any consent that may be required under subsection (1)(c)"; a consent required only under (1)(a) or (b) is outside it
        IF NOT `the consent is one that may be required under subsection (1)(c)` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (an "on the application" condition read like "upon", ruling rule (c); marginal reading M7): "on the application of the parties to a contract"
        IF NOT `the parties to the contract have applied` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", marginal reading M5): "if it is satisfied that it cannot reasonably be ascertained whether or not the third party has in fact relied on the term of the contract"
        -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): the satisfaction of the court or tribunal is a judgment handed to it, and the person has not stated it
        OTHERWISE `the court or tribunal is satisfied that it cannot reasonably be ascertained whether or not the third party has in fact relied on the term`

-- src:169 | (6) If the court or arbitral tribunal dispenses with a third party’s
-- src:170 | consent, it may impose such conditions as it thinks fit, including a
-- src:171 | condition requiring the payment of compensation to the third party.
@ref s 3(6) (src:169-171)
GIVEN `the court or arbitral tribunal has dispensed with the third party's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(6) the court or arbitral tribunal may impose such conditions as it thinks fit` MEANS
    IF `the court or arbitral tribunal has dispensed with the third party's consent`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (a failed "if", marginal reading M5): "If the court or arbitral tribunal dispenses with a third party's consent, it may impose such conditions as it thinks fit"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

@ref s 3(6) (src:169-171)
GIVEN `the court or arbitral tribunal has dispensed with the third party's consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(6) the court or arbitral tribunal may impose a condition requiring the payment of compensation to the third party` MEANS
    `s 3(6) the court or arbitral tribunal may impose such conditions as it thinks fit` `the court or arbitral tribunal has dispensed with the third party's consent`

-- src:173 | (7) The jurisdiction conferred on the court by subsections (4), (5)
-- src:174 | and (6) is exercisable by both the General Division of the High Court
-- src:175 | and a District Court.
@ref s 3(7) (src:173-175)
GIVEN `the body` IS A `Forum`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 3(7) the jurisdiction conferred on the court by subsections (4), (5) and (6) is exercisable by this body` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `the General Division of the High Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a District Court` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "exercisable by both the General Division of the High Court and a District Court" is not closed with "only", so another court is neither included nor excluded
    WHEN `another court` THEN NOTHING
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 3(7) speaks of "the jurisdiction conferred on the court"; the power of an arbitral tribunal is given by subsections (4) to (6) themselves
    WHEN `an arbitral tribunal` THEN NOTHING

§ `Regulative rules derived from the answers above (no time limit is stated, so none is given)`

-- Ruling N2: where the text names who bears a prohibition, the prohibition (SHANT) is derived from the answer.
-- The text names "the parties to the contract" and states no period; a SHANT with no WITHIN stands until an act
-- breaches it.  A DEONTIC value cannot be compared in an #ASSERT on this binary, so the tests assert the decision
-- function above, and the #TRACEs in the test file are read by eye (NOTES.md, "What the main binary does not accept").
-- src:110 | 3.—(1) Subject to this section, where a third party has a right under
-- src:111 | section 2 to enforce a term of the contract, the parties to the contract
-- src:113 | may not, by agreement, rescind the contract, or vary the contract in
-- src:114 | such a way as to extinguish or alter the third party’s entitlement under
-- src:115 | that right, without the third party’s consent if —
@ref s 3(1) the prohibition (src:110-115)
GIVEN `the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce the term` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `what the parties do` IS A `What the parties do by agreement`
      `the third party has consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the express term of the contract about consent` IS AN `Express term of the contract about consent`
      `the circumstances the contract specifies exist` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 3(1) the parties to the contract SHANT rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent` MEANS
    IF `s 3(1) with (3) the parties to the contract may not rescind or vary the contract without the third party's consent, taking an express term of the contract into account` `the third party has a right under section 2 to enforce the term` `what the parties do` `the third party has consented` `one of the circumstances in (a), (b) and (c) exists` `the express term of the contract about consent` `the circumstances the contract specifies exist` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN (PARTY `the parties to the contract` SHANT `rescind the contract by agreement without the third party's consent`)
         RAND (PARTY `the parties to the contract` SHANT `vary the contract by agreement without the third party's consent so as to extinguish or alter the third party's entitlement`)
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:147 | (4) Where the consent of a third party is required under
-- src:148 | subsection (1) or (3), the court or arbitral tribunal may, on the
-- src:149 | application of the parties to the contract, dispense with such consent if
-- src:150 | the court or tribunal is satisfied that —
-- src:152 | (a) the consent cannot be obtained because the third party’s
-- src:153 | whereabouts cannot reasonably be ascertained; or
-- src:160 | (b) the third party is mentally incapable of giving the third
-- src:161 | party’s consent.
@ref s 3(4) the court's permission (src:147-161)
GIVEN `the consent of the third party is required under subsection (1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties to the contract have applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court or tribunal is satisfied that the consent cannot be obtained because the third party's whereabouts cannot reasonably be ascertained` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the court or tribunal is satisfied that the third party is mentally incapable of giving the third party's consent` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under the Act` `Act under the Act`
`s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal MAY dispense with the third party's consent` MEANS
    IF `s 3(4) the court or arbitral tribunal may dispense with the third party's consent` `the consent of the third party is required under subsection (1) or (3)` `the parties to the contract have applied` `the court or tribunal is satisfied that the consent cannot be obtained because the third party's whereabouts cannot reasonably be ascertained` `the court or tribunal is satisfied that the third party is mentally incapable of giving the third party's consent` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `the court or arbitral tribunal` MAY `dispense with the third party's consent`
    ELSE FULFILLED
